description:
Run any number of inputs as one queued sequence, stopping at the first
click, drag, key press, or scroll that produces no screen change.

Use this when you are CONFIDENT of several inputs in a row — confirm
dialogs, a decided card sequence, walking a chosen map path, shopping a
decided list. Each step executes in order and the screen must react to
it; a click/drag/key/scroll that changes nothing ABORTS the remaining
steps so a misread screen cannot cascade. Never queue through an
outcome you have not seen before (unknown fights, unread rewards).

Steps are objects with a "do" field:
  {"do": "left_click", "x": 640, "y": 300}
  {"do": "right_click", "x": 640, "y": 300}
  {"do": "left_click_drag", "x1": 400, "y1": 700, "x2": 640, "y2": 400}
  {"do": "mouse_move", "x": 640, "y": 300}
  {"do": "key", "keys": "Return"}
  {"do": "scroll", "x": 640, "y": 400, "direction": "down", "amount": 3}
  {"do": "wait", "seconds": 2}

Returns a text log of what ran (and what was skipped, if aborted) plus
ONE screenshot of the final settled screen — intermediate frames are
deliberately dropped to keep your context lean.
